WEBVTT

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.600
Shiori-san.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.730
Sou-kun...

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.450
Is Kaori...

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.110
It seems her condition has stabilized.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.830
I see.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.660
But...

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.480
They said there's virtually no hope that she'll ever wake up.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.690
<i>At that point, the planetarium café was the last thing on our minds,</i>

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.170
<i>and ultimately, we ended up doing nothing for that year's school festival.</i>

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:10.760
<i>Immediately after that,</i>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.640
<i>we heard from Nagisa-senpai that
Furukawa Yui had transferred away.</i>

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.680
Ooh, I found you!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.920
You should at least make a token visit
to club every now and then, you know.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.850
Sorry.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.940
The class dean's concerned about you.
Keeps asking about your career choice.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.860
Oh, yeah, that...

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.980
Sou, I understand how you feel,
but you need to switch gears.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.840
Yeah.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.780
Speaking of which,
what did you decide to do, Prez?

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.770
I've chosen the Department of Science
at Uchihama U.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.500
My recommendation.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.000
Nagisa-san.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.420
I also intend to do whatever I can.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:54.530
What will <i>you</i> do, Sou-san?

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.020
I...

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.030
<i>In order to find a way to make Kaori better,</i>

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.690
<i>I set my sights on studying medicine.</i>

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.240
<i>Shortly after being accepted into medical school,</i>

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.670
<i>I left the house where my memories with Kaori still lingered.</i>

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.690
<i>At the university, I immediately ran into a wall.</i>

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.290
<i>Brain research was vital to bringing Kaori back.</i>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.360
<i>But I came to the hard realization
that modern medicine was limited</i>

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.340
<i>by its focus on the treatment of symptoms.</i>

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.480
<i>The brain was unknown territory.</i>

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.020
<i>Other parts that were injured could be artificially substituted—</i>

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.750
<i>or, in theory, possibly even regrown—</i>

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.340
<i>but the brain alone remained irreplaceable.</i>

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.740
You know, I'm doing research on
quantum Turing machines right now.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.400
Quantum Turing machines?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.010
Don't you remember that teacher we had in high school who used to ignore the course material

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.250
to ramble on about whatever?

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.620
Sure.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.780
Back then, I thought that the stuff he talked about didn't make any sense,

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.430
but my research now is essentially about getting that off paper and into practice.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.690
Well, to put it simply,

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.170
the idea is that maybe the brain is a quantum Turing machine,

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.440
or something along those lines.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:33.730
The brain?

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.780
<i>Ready to grasp at straws,
I got into quantum theory</i>

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.900
<i>and even into a field
called quantum cybernetics.</i>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:51.580
<i>It was only later that I found out that it was closely related to Shiori-san's field of study.</i>

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.520
<i>All I'd heard was that since Kaori's accident,</i>

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.540
<i>she had immersed herself
in some kind of special research.</i>

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.010
<i>A few years passed,
but Kaori remained unconscious.</i>

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.860
Sou, if you're home, I'm coming in.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.070
It's so gloomy in here.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:24.910
Again.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.440
I'm gonna use your kitchen.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.930
Kenny sent over another new report.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.330
What was it again?

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:41.000
"Reverse Time Travel by Extending Cosmic Strings into Extra Dimensions," I think it was?

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.810
Talk about a pipe dream, right?

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.960
I mean, it's basically talking about traveling back in time.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.390
Even if that were hypothetically possible...

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.710
What about time paradoxes?
No one knows what'd cause them, right?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.980
It's from Nagisa-san.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.570
Ah, my dear old alma mater...

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:13.680
But why are you building a new research lab here?

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.750
There's nothing really wrong
with the current location, is there?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.640
Do you remember, Airi-san?

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.250
About that black box that I often brought to the club room?

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:24.090
I do...

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.780
That box has been the subject of research since back then,

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.560
but as it was studied, it became clear that it responded strongly to a specific location.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.720
It did?

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.790
Yes.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.620
And that location is here?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.440
That's right.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.420
Why is that?

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.730
Not to mention, isn't demolishing the entire academy just for this research kind of overkill?

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.660
Would you two grant me a little more of your time?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.000
Sure, I guess that's fine...

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.270
What is this place?

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.820
The Hanamiya General Research Laboratory.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.000
This is where we're researching that black cube.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:15.600
We also do globally cutting-edge work
in various other fields.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.960
Shiori-san...

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.560
Long time no see, Sou-kun.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.160
You too, Airi-san. Welcome.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.000
It's been a long time.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.760
Shiori-san, is it ready for us to show them now?

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:28.530
Yes.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.090
What is this place?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.760
It's where the lab's top secret research is conducted.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.930
Is this where you work, Shiori-san?

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.920
Yes. I'm a member of the research team.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.560
What in the world are you researching?

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.750
Well...

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.260
It'll be faster if you see it for yourself.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.800
Wow, this is pretty impressive.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.510
It's practically science fiction.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.420
So the thing in the center is top secret?

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.660
That's right.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.420
Yui...

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.020
What?

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.520
Is that... Furukawa?!

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.030
Huh? What?!

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:08.780
Yes.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.150
That is Yui-san.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.660
Or no, perhaps I should say
it's what <i>used</i> to be Yui-san.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.410
Why? What's Yui doing here?

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.820
Yui-san was...

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:23.440
On that day—the day Kaori-san
was in that accident—

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.630
I returned home to find Yui-san asleep.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.630
Or to be precise, I suppose I should say that she had ceased to function.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.680
Yui-san, I didn't know you'd returned home.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.870
Today was a terrible day, you know.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.990
Don't you start worrying me too—

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:58.870
What?!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:02.900
It can't be...

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.670
Sakunoshin! Sakunoshin!

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.480
Please! Come quickly!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.420
Kaori said she'd lost this.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:14.430
Why did Yui have it?

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.180
I don't know.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:19.350
I don't know whether Yui-san was related to that accident or what.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.200
But why is this top secret?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.230
She is...

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.690
not human.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.440
What?!

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.820
Not human?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.490
To put it simply, she's an artificial humanoid.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.990
An artificial humanoid...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:40.560
She is something we could never build with our current technology.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.960
So who could have made her?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:47.340
Why did she appear at Uchihama Academy and then suddenly cease to operate?

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.880
We have nothing but questions.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.590
But why have you kept this quiet until now?

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:01.560
Back then, with what happened to Kaori-san,
I didn't have the courage to tell the rest of you.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.380
I'm sorry.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.310
And there was one other reason.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:12.530
The black cube, which our research team calls the AI Unit, responded to Yui-san.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.900
Yui and that box... Just how could they be related?

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:24.040
But as we studied her,
I found one possible way to save Kaori.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.600
A possible way to save Kaori?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.000
How?

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.520
We found that Yui-san had a flawless set
of artificial vital systems.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:35.590
Internal organs, blood vessels,
the nervous system, and even the brain.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.010
The brain...

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:37.680
That's right.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:42.320
Her brain has functionality
that equals that of a human brain.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.390
Then, the way you thought to save Kaori is...

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:50.290
We study her body and build a new one.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.770
And then we transfer Kaori to it.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.590
Transfer Kaori...

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.930
All the information in the brain.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.030
We'd transfer it all over,
including her consciousness.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.010
A quantum Turing machine...

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.420
But that's...

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.350
Is that even theoretically possible?

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:10.210
We were hoping the two of you
could assist us with the research.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.970
<i>Airi and I dropped out of university to join Shiori-san's team,</i>

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.470
<i>and we began the research toward building a new synthetic body.</i>

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.470
<i>It was named the Yui's
Unforced Intelligence System.</i>

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.520
<i>The YUIs Project.</i>

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.060
<i>Airi mainly worked on the AI Unit,</i>

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.860
<i>while I studied Yui's body.</i>

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:44.640
<i>The technology that had been used
to build Yui's body was astonishing.</i>

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.950
<i>Our research progressed by leaps and bounds.</i>

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.720
<i>After several more years had passed,</i>

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.560
<i>we had finally completed a new synthetic body.</i>

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.340
The time has finally come.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:12.650
Yes.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:16.680
We will now perform Sasaki Kaori's consciousness transfer.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:17.650
Please begin.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.240
Connecting interface.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.100
Quantum oscillations confirmed.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.160
Commencing quantum entanglement.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.120
Brain waves, normal.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.970
Heart rate, normal.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.300
The synthetic body's functions have begun to activate as well.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:32.690
Huh?

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.760
What's wrong?

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.320
I don't know, but...

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:41.130
Um, the information isn't transferring over to the synthetic body's artificial brain.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:42.850
Why not?

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.390
Wh-What should we do?

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.320
This can't be...

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.510
It wasn't supposed to be like this...

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.810
Stop the machine! Cancel the transplant!

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.020
Quantum entanglement disengaged.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.350
What could this be?

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:00.190
What is it?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.510
Kaori-san's consciousness hasn't been transferred,

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:06.780
but the synthetic body shows signs of an active consciousness.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.220
The experiment?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.570
A failure.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.640
We can't use this synthetic body for the transplant anymore.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.300
Sou, is it true that Shiori-san's going overseas?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.620
Yeah.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:26.320
There's apparently a place in Northern Europe
where they're doing research into artificial brains.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.220
I see.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.090
So Shiori-san hasn't given up yet.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.540
But the method you used is...

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:34.320
Yeah.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.460
Well, I'm going to head back.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.540
What do you suppose those two are going to do?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:01.010
If Akiyama-kun doesn't arrive at a conclusion soon,

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.920
it's going to be unfortunate for Hasekura-san.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:08.100
After all, Akiyama-san's thoughts
have been so consumed with Kaori-san

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.890
that it doesn't seem like he's noticed Hasekura-san's feelings for him.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:16.050
I'd thought the failure of the experiment would be a good place to stop, but...

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:20.650
It's not so simple. That's how relationships between a man and a woman are.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:23.530
This is why the three-dimensional
world is such a pain.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.150
Right, Hiro?

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:52.760
"Reverse Time Travel by Extending Cosmic Strings into Extra Dimensions..."

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:56.850
I mean, it's basically talking about traveling back in time.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.690
Traveling back in time...

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:03.870
She is something we could never build with our current technology.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.070
Impossible technology...

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:11.620
You know, I'm doing research on
quantum Turing machines right now.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:13.490
It can't be...

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.430
That black box that I often
brought to the club room?

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.800
As it was studied,

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.730
it became clear that it responded strongly to a specific location.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.710
This is absurd.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.220
It's ridiculous!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.560
It should be ridiculous, and yet...

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.980
What's with how neatly it all adds up?

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.440
Hasekura-san.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.110
Alone again today?

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.790
Yeah, I guess.

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.920
Is Akiyama-san still keeping himself locked away?

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.120
What in the world could he be doing?

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.800
Wake up, Sou.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.560
Kaori...

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.340
Wrong.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.590
Oh, it's you, Airi.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.880
Do you always sleep in places like this?

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.100
Got a problem with that?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.850
It's not really a problem,
but it can't be good for you.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.450
Oh, this is perfect.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.480
There's something I want you to see.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.480
Hm? What is it?

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:34.500
Why...

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:37.570
What in the world do you think you're doing?!

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.040
Kaori's synthetic body has been made into Yui...

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.160
It's been remodeled to look like Yui's body?

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.090
We're going to change the past and save Kaori.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:48.400
Change the past?

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.570
We'll send Yui to right before Kaori gets into that accident

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:53.990
and have her prevent it.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.730
H-Hold on a second.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.440
Don't tell me you're talking about time travel?

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.720
That stuff's pure fiction!

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:01.520
Wha—

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.100
This is...

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.380
the paper by that American researcher
that Kenny sent long ago?

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.160
Yeah.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:11.520
This is pure theory. It doesn't have a shred of evidence to back it up.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:14.610
You seriously believe it's possible to travel back in time?

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.630
Yeah.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.050
Even if this were hypothetically real,

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:21.840
and Yui were to change the past,
it would only cause the world to diverge.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.160
It wouldn't mean that the
current Kaori would be saved.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.980
After the world diverges,

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.940
there's a chance it'll merge
back together again.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.210
Merge back?

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.420
The chains of fate would rectify the world

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.500
and the paradox would eventually vanish.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.800
The chains of fate...?

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:43.480
Airi, do you really believe that every time a physicist conducts that cat experiment somewhere,

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.970
the physical quantity of universes doubles?

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.820
But that's the many-worlds interpretation, right?

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:54.320
Compared to the overwhelming
scale of the universe,

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.810
they're glitches that can be cleared up
within just a couple decades.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:01.590
Once the report becomes lost and the experimenter's memory fades away,

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.580
the world merges back together.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:06.850
In order to make efficient use of resources,

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:10.770
a force will exert itself to once again merge worlds that have diverged.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.050
That's nature's law.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:15.110
And that's what you're calling "the chains of fate"?

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:20.660
B-But in order to go into the past using that method,

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.360
you need a quantum oscillation device on the other side, t—

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.430
You don't think...

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:26.690
The AI Unit?

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:31.660
That cube generates minute quantum oscillations at one specific location.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.440
And where it responds most strongly

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.700
is here, where the elevator stood on the fifth floor of the old school building.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.160
The location where Yui appeared...

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.080
That's right.

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:44.420
What is Yui to begin with, anyway?

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.240
Created with impossible technology,

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:50.540
she suddenly appeared and responded to this black box—the AI Unit.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.100
For what purpose was she there?

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.780
What was her goal? Her motivation?

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.120
Did she really have amnesia then?

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.220
Thinking back now,

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.390
even her incomprehensible actions all add up if my hypothesis is right!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:06.350
Sou, are you... in your right mind?

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:08.350
Who knows?

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.830
Sou... Airi...

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.260
Listen, Yui. This is a ball.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.140
A ball.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.480
Ball.

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:24.740
Then... what's this?

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.830
Ball?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.580
So close! This is a globe.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.840
Globe... Globe?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.910
Yes! A globe!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.510
Come on.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:44.300
Left. Right. Left. Right.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.600
Sou, this is dangerous.
This is very dangerous.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.380
It's okay. It's very okay.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.360
The air is clear today.

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.040
The starlight that we see from the Earth's surface

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.070
is light from long, long ago.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.630
For example, take a look there.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:09.280
The distance between the Andromeda Galaxy there
and Earth is 2.39 million light-years.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:14.090
What we're seeing now is light
that's a whole 2.39 million years old.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:18.070
Compared to 2.39 million years,

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.980
fourteen years is but the blink of an eye.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:27.280
The more time passes,
the more distant the past becomes,

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.460
increasing the amount of energy we'll need.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.720
Based on the simulations so far,

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:33.760
the efficiency is worse than we expected.

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:52.240
Why?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.280
You look like it's the end of the world.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.390
Why won't it work?

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:18.610
Hey, Sou, who do you suppose
made the very first Yui?

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.230
The AI Unit.

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.080
What?

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.010
Ultimately, in the beginning,
while analyzing that cube, we...

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:28.400
Or rather, I think Shiori-san
might have created her.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:30.380
Then, what about the AI Unit?

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.040
I don't know.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:37.650
That quantum Turing machine might be something like the Akashic records,

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:40.340
meant to record data on the many worlds.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:44.790
Which is exactly why it responds only to Yui,
who is the point of divergence,

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:47.110
and permits no one but Yui
to travel back through time,

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.050
serving as her save point...

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:53.560
That's it! A save point!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.420
Yui.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.170
Yes.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.050
I'm going to send you into the past now.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.070
Understood.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:09.490
Your job is to save Sasaki Kaori from the accident that takes place on October 14th.

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:10.830
Understood.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:14.830
Yui, I...

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:18.590
Sou...

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:23.200
I'm sorry.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.350
Maybe we should go see what's going on.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:28.480
I agree.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:30.770
I'll hold the fort here.

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:32.950
All right, then let's split up and check things out.

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:35.300
Uh, then I'll go upstairs.

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.490
Sou-kun?

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.820
Sou-kun, what's wrong?

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:53.730
Kaori...

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:28.330
How many times has it been for me since then?

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:29.370
I heard there's been another case in the neighborhood.

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:31.080
I want to tell you everything right this minute.

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:31.820
Open the door!
I want to tell you everything right this minute.

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:33.540
It doesn't matter who I fall in love with, does it?

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:34.280
About Yui-chan...

00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:36.590
You will not find happiness!

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:40.220
Episode ten: "The Time Remaining."
